# Obsidian logistic model (bootstrap).
#
# Hand-calibrated from the deterministic checks' known-good thresholds so the ML
# layer is sensible on day one. It is intentionally conservative: no single
# feature crosses the flag threshold on its own, so the model only speaks up when
# several signals agree. Collect labelled data with dataset-logging + /ob label,
# then replace this with a trained model via ml/train/LogisticTrainer.
#
# Feature order (see Features.java):
#   reach_mean_excess, reach_viol_ratio, angle_mean, angle_viol_ratio,
#   click_mean_ms, click_sigma_ms, click_autocorr, aim_micro_fraction,
#   max_distinct_targets, mace_combo_sigma_ms
obsidian-model 1
mean -0.2,0.03,18,0.03,160,45,0.05,0.35,1.0,150
scale 0.4,0.2,20,0.2,80,30,0.3,0.3,1.0,80
weight 0.9,1.6,0.6,1.3,-0.7,-1.0,1.0,-1.1,1.4,-0.6
bias -2.6
